<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Hunt</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 14)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>hunt &lt;player or monster&gt;
hunt               (again, to stop hunting)
</pre>
<p>Hunt is tracking that does the walking for you. You study the ground for 
your prey's tracks, and if you can read them, you set off after them by 
yourself, step after step, wherever they lead in the world: you search 
for hidden exits and open doors on the way. When you catch up, you attack.
</p><p>Your track and hunt skills together decide whether you can read the 
trail, with your brain and level against your prey's. You read it again 
at every step, so you may lose it on the way. Each step costs endurance, 
more in cities, indoors and on ice than in the open, and when you are too 
tired you stop. You must be standing, and you can't hunt on water. The 
trail ends where your prey enters something, such as a ship or a cart.
</p><p>To attack a player you find, both of you must have signed the Book of 
Blood.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
